  "id": "moving-window-technique",
  "term": "moving-window technique",
  "definition": "The moving-window technique is a research method that limits what a person can see to a small movable area on a visual display. In psychology studies, it is used to track which parts of a stimulus someone actively examines and can serve as a more direct measure of attention than standard eye-tracking in some tasks.",
